    "source": "HouseBets Hubie's Road, stated in three places, each read in the game's code or answers, none on a rendered page (DL-11): in the game settings the site loads — the fairness answer, E01 \"return\" (GET /housegames/road/fairness): \"99% for every difficulty and every stopping rule: C(25 − m, k) / C(25, k) is the chance that k lanes are all safe\", requested by the road game bundle (platform-housegames-road-game.js sha256 d9ba3797255b6729…, the file E02 cites: jt(\"/\"+rq+\"/fairness\") then setFairnessSpec; that the live road page loads this bundle is inferred, bundles/LIVE-BUNDLES.md 10 Oct 2026); and in the rules — the game page rules panel in that bundle, E02 rulesRoadReturn (game page rules panel): \"Every way of playing returns {pct}% (1% house edge). After k lanes with m sharks the multiplier is 0.99 × C(25, k) / C(25 − m, k), the fair price of surviving k lanes, less 1%. Payouts are rounded down to the wallet’s smallest unit.\" (its {pct} is filled at run time, not captured rendered; the figure read is the stated house edge); and, since HouseBets reworded rulesRoadReturn on 16 Oct, in the live copy of that bundle, E08 rulesRoadReturn (game page rules panel, live copy of 19 Oct): \"Theoretical RTP before rounding and any payout cap: {pct}% (1% house edge). A capped payout can reduce the return. After k lanes with m sharks the multiplier is 0.99 × C(25, k) / C(25 − m, k), the fair price of surviving k lanes, less 1%. Payouts are rounded down to the wallet’s smallest unit.\" (E08). Held to the highest figure stated: game settings 0.99, rules 0.99, rules 0.99 (they agree)."
